# UWE host update — allow the service user to start ONLY the root-owned update unit.
# Installed by deploy/scripts/setup-uwe-host.sh as /etc/sudoers.d/uwe-host-update
#
# Security: NEVER grant sudo on a script that lives in the uwe-writable repo
# (/opt/uwe/deploy/scripts/*). A compromised uwe account could rewrite that file
# and gain root. Instead sudo is scoped to the fixed, root-owned systemctl binary
# starting one specific, root-owned unit. The unit's ExecStart (uwe-host-update.sh)
# still re-checks UWE_HOST_UPDATE_ENABLED and a fresh request file before doing work.
#
# Validate after install: visudo -cf /etc/sudoers.d/uwe-host-update
Defaults!/usr/bin/systemctl !requiretty
uwe ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemctl start uwe-host-update.service
# Callers: deploy/scripts/uwe-host-update-trigger.sh (guards + escalation) and
# uwe-cd-trigger.sh (SSH CD path) both write a request file, then invoke the
# systemctl command above via sudo. The Studio host-update service
# (packages/database/src/host-update-service.ts) must invoke the same command.
